<h1 class="article-title">Auction Announced for Property at Eksporta Street 3 in the Liepaja Industrial Park</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>As the development of the Liepaja Industrial Park on the site of the former “Liepājas metalurgs” steelworks continues, the Liepaja Special Economic Zone (Liepaja SEZ) Authority has announced an auction for the property at Eksporta Street 3, located within the Liepaja Industrial Park. This is the next step in involving businesses in the regeneration and transformation of the industrial area, offering an opportunity to acquire existing production buildings together with the land.</p><p>The Liepaja Special Economic Zone Authority is organizing an electronic ascending-bid auction for the newly created property at Eksporta Street 3, Liepaja.</p><p>Auction property</p><ul><li>Address: Eksporta Street 3, Liepaja</li><li>Land area: 51,521 m²</li><li>Buildings: the plot contains buildings and structures, including warehouses of various sizes, a production workshop building, a workshop building and other structures</li><li>Starting price: EUR 680,000.00</li><li>Bid increment: EUR 6,800.00</li><li>Security deposit: EUR 68,000.00</li></ul><p>The following conditions apply to the auction:</p><ul><li>the building(s) must be renovated and/or reconstructed and the surrounding area improved within 60 (sixty) months from the date of signing the purchase agreement;</li><li>the buildings must comply with the minimum energy-efficiency requirements established by the laws and regulations of the Republic of Latvia;</li><li>minimum investment of EUR 733,076.85 (seven hundred and thirty-three thousand seventy-six euros and 85 cents) must be made in the auction property.</li></ul><p>The auction opens at 13:00 on 6 October 2026 and closes at 13:00 on 5 November 2026. Applicants may register for the auction from 13:00 on 6 October 2026 until 23:59 on 26 October 2026 on the electronic auction platform: <a href="https://izsoles.ta.gov.lv">izsoles.ta.gov.lv</a>.</p><p>The auction will be conducted electronically on <a href="https://izsoles.ta.gov.lv">izsoles.ta.gov.lv</a>.</p><p>The Liepaja SEZ Authority initially consolidated all the properties located on the site of the former steelworks, worked together with the municipality to develop a detailed local planning document for the area, and constructed the first roads with the necessary utility infrastructure. The disposal of properties through auctions is the next step in involving businesses in the regeneration and transformation of the industrial area, offering them the opportunity to acquire existing production buildings together with land and renovate and redevelop them in line with the requirements of a modern green economy business environment.</p><p>The Liepaja Industrial Park is located within the territory of the Liepaja Special Economic Zone. It is a location for modern manufacturing facilities, science and research, logistics centers and the development of energy-intensive projects. The approximately 120-hectare development area has been divided into individual plots offering development opportunities and access to utility infrastructure.</p><p>The Liepaja Industrial Park is being developed by the Liepaja SEZ Authority and the Liepaja Municipality. The park borders Lake Liepaja, a specially protected nature area included in the NATURA 2000 network. According to the approved development strategy, the aim is to attract more than EUR 275 million in private investment and create at least 1,500 new jobs.</p><p>Sustainability is embedded in the “genetic code” of the Liepaja Industrial Park, with education, innovation and circular economy principles clearly established as its foundations.</p></div>
